
Usage: /TALK <username>
  Start  a  private  chat with <username>.  To talk with more than one
  user  just  separate  the  usernames with ","s.  /TALK only supports
  ANSI  color,  so if your terminal doesn't support it, you are out of
  luck.   The  window  where  you type will be the bottom one, and all
  other  users  will  be  ontop.  Normally, the topmost window will be
  where  all output from channel activities will be displayed.  If you
  want  don't  want  this  window  opened,  simply set the environment
  variable  TALKOUTWINHEIGHT to 0.  The windows of the other users you
  are chatting with will have their windows labelled with their names,
  in  the  form  of  "<<< Name >>>" or ">>> Name <<<".  "<<< Name >>>"
  indicates  that the user is not in chat mode with you, and ">>> Name
  <<<" indicates they are.

  To exit press ^D or /WIN CLOSE.

  Other special keys are:

  Key       Action
  ---       --------------------------------------
  ^A        Move cursor to beginning of line
  ^B        Clear to bottom of window
  <BS>      Delete character to the left of cursor
  ^G        Beep the screen
  ^K        Clear to end of line
  ^L        Redraw screen
  ^U        Clear line
  ^X        Clear screen
  ^Y        Delete line
  ^Z        Move cursor to the end of line
  ^[[A      Move cursor up one line
  ^[[B      Move cursor down one line
  ^[[C      Move cursor one position right
  ^[[D      Move cursor one position left
  <DEL>     Delete character under cursor

  note:
  ^x = hold down the CTRL key and type <x>
  ^[[A..^[[D are generated by the cursor keys on your keyboard

  Example:
     /TALK larry,moe,curry

  See Also:
     /SETENV TALKOUTWINHEIGHT QUITAFTERTALK
